<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/_house.css">
<style>
.root { gap: 28px; }
.flowstrip { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink2); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 14px; }
.card.code .d { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--code); }
.card.code { background: var(--elevated); }
.cardlogo { height: 24px; opacity: 0.85; margin-left: 12px; }
</style>
<style>@page { size: 900,00pt 363,00pt; margin: 0 }</style></head>
<body>
<h1>Fuzzy sets: reasoning with degrees of truth</h1>

<div class="col root"><div class="row"><div class="card blue"><div class="t">cold</div><div class="d">1.0 up to 12 °C</div>
<div class="d">0 from 22 °C</div></div>
<div class="card green"><div class="t">warm</div><div class="d">0 at 15 °C, full 22 to 28 °C</div>
<div class="d">back to 0 at 35 °C</div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">hot</div><div class="d">0 up to 30 °C</div>
<div class="d">1.0 from 38 °C</div></div></div>
<div class="row"><div class="card green"><div class="t">IF temp IS warm AND rising</div><div class="d">THEN reduce heating slightly</div>
<div class="d">fires at degree 0.72 - no cliff</div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">no hard threshold:</div><div class="d">19°C is 60% warm,</div>
<div class="d">28% cold - rules blend by degree</div></div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="d">membership: 0 · 0.25 · 0.5 · 0.75 · 1.0</div>
<div class="d">temperature (°C): 0 · 10 · 20 · 30 · 40</div>
<div class="d">original figure · fuzzy logic after Zadeh 1965 · degrees instead of two states</div></div></div>


</body>
</html>
